nment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:1b6021a31295a137f8f485e34ae2001ea30cb695f447a3379cdc3e6d98a6f05e","file":"preprints/Bounded-recovery-for-modular-spectral-averages-September-23-2026/build/sections/04-bounded-recovery.tex","line":20,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"00a1986b88a636000d4f5629af1beed3b107342e9b266300fb181940fcacd353","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Bounded-recovery-for-modular-spectral-averages-September-23-2026/build/sections/04-bounded-recovery.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:1b6021a31295a137f8f485e34ae2001ea30cb695f447a3379cdc3e6d98a6f05e","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Bounded-recovery-for-modular-spectral-averages-September-23-2026/build/sections/04-bounded-recovery.tex#L20"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{rec:bounded}\nLet $M$ be a von Neumann algebra with a faithful normal state $\\phi$ such\nthat $M_\\phi=\\C1$.  Use the standard-space notation and the fixed mean $m$\nof \\Cref{mod:average}.  Fix $T\\in\\B(H)$ and $s\\in\\R$.  Suppose that\n$\\delta_n>0$ tends to zero and that $h_n\\in H$ are unit vectors with\n$D$-spectral support in $[s-\\delta_n,s+\\delta_n]$.  If\n\\begin{equation}\n\\label{eq:recovery-positive}\n \\limsup_{n\\to\\infty}m_t\\norm{TU_th_n}^{2}>0,\n\\end{equation}\nthen there are a subsequence $(n_j)$, elements $v_j\\in M$, and constants\n$C_*<\\infty$ and $\\eta>0$ such that, for every $j$,\n\\[\n \\norm{v_j}\\le C_*,\\qquad\n \\norm{Tv_j\\xi}\\ge\\eta,\n\\]\nand $v_j\\xi$ has $D$-spectral support in\n$[s-4\\delta_{n_j},s+4\\delta_{n_j}]$."}
